<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Equipment traders for the Twitch Allies — the economy behind their docks.

  THE PROBLEM THIS SOLVES. A wharf / shipyard / equipment dock does not conjure
  shields, engines, weapons and software out of nothing — it makes them from
  COMPONENTS, and those components are flown in by the owning faction's equipment
  traders. `<basket basket="equipment">` is the 11 wares that feed exactly this:
  advancedelectronics, antimatterconverters, claytronics, dronecomponents, fieldcoils,
  missilecomponents, shieldcomponents, smartchips, turretcomponents, weaponcomponents,
  khaakalloy (libraries/baskets.xml). No components in storage, no equipment on the
  shelf. Vanilla defines exactly twelve such jobs in libraries/jobs.xml — an L and an M for each economic
  faction (argon, antigone, paranid, holyorder, teladi, ministry) — and you can watch
  one work in x4debug.txt: `'HOP High-Tech Trader Hermes Sentinel' (job:
  'holyorder_equipment_trader_m')`.

  twitchally had none, so a station chat built listed every ship hull (those are
  built to order) and no equipment at all (that needs components on hand). Nothing
  was wrong with the blueprints or the licences — the shop had no raw material, and
  nothing was ever going to bring it any.

  COPIED FROM `argon_equipment_trader_m` / `_l`, with three deliberate changes:

  * `buildatshipyard="false" gate="true"`. Vanilla builds its traders AT A SHIPYARD
    OF THE OWNING FACTION. twitchally has no shipyard, so with vanilla's `true` the
    quota could never be filled and not one trader would ever exist. `false` +
    `gate="true"` spawns them at a gate instead — the same escape hatch the Kha'ak
    jobs use, they have no shipyards either.
  * `<select faction="argon" …>` picks the HULL. Ship selection by faction goes
    through the ware <owner> lists, which name no Twitch faction — so selecting by
    `twitchally` would find no ship. `<owner exact="twitchally">` still hands the
    finished ship to the right faction. This is the same split our MD spawns already
    use (an Argon hull, a Twitch owner) and it is known to work.
  * `<location>` drops vanilla's `faction="argon" relation="ally"` filter. That
    restricts an Argon trader to Argon-friendly space; twitchally is +1 with every
    faction in the game (see factions.xml), so the filter would be a no-op written
    out longhand. Galaxy-wide is the same thing, said plainly.

  Quotas are deliberately well under Argon's (10 galaxy / 3 cluster / 3 sector for
  the M): these ships are pure logistics for a handful of viewer-built stations, not
  a full faction economy, and every one of them is a ship the player has to share
  the sector with.

  The name refs {20204,401} / {20204,301} are vanilla's own "Equipment Transport"
  job names, reused the way this mod already reuses Argon colours and icons.
-->
<diff>
  <add sel="/jobs">
    <job id="twitchally_equipment_trader_m" name="{20204,401}">
      <modifiers rebuild="false" commandeerable="true" />
      <orders>
        <order order="TradeRoutine" default="true">
          <param name="minbuy" value="0" />
          <param name="maxbuy" value="5" />
          <param name="minsell" value="0" />
          <param name="maxsell" value="5" />
        </order>
      </orders>
      <basket basket="equipment" />
      <category faction="twitchally" tags="[factionlogic, freighter, trader]" size="ship_m" />
      <quota galaxy="6" cluster="2" />
      <location class="galaxy" macro="xu_ep2_universe_macro" />
      <environment buildatshipyard="false" gate="true" />
      <ship>
        <select faction="argon" tags="[trader, container]" size="ship_m" />
        <loadout>
          <quantity exact="1.0" />
          <quality exact="0.71">
            <variation exact="0.5" />
          </quality>
        </loadout>
        <owner exact="twitchally" overridenpc="true" />
      </ship>
    </job>

    <job id="twitchally_equipment_trader_l" name="{20204,301}">
      <modifiers rebuild="false" commandeerable="true" />
      <orders>
        <order order="TradeRoutine" default="true">
          <param name="minbuy" value="0" />
          <param name="maxbuy" value="5" />
          <param name="minsell" value="0" />
          <param name="maxsell" value="5" />
        </order>
      </orders>
      <basket basket="equipment" />
      <category faction="twitchally" tags="[factionlogic, freighter, trader]" size="ship_l" />
      <quota galaxy="2" cluster="1" />
      <location class="galaxy" macro="xu_ep2_universe_macro" />
      <environment buildatshipyard="false" gate="true" />
      <ship>
        <select faction="argon" tags="[trader, container]" size="ship_l" />
        <loadout>
          <quantity exact="1.0" />
          <quality exact="0.71">
            <variation exact="0.5" />
          </quality>
        </loadout>
        <owner exact="twitchally" overridenpc="true" />
      </ship>
    </job>
  </add>
</diff>
